WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
Two countries short of water.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.950
Singapore, an island city-state off the
southern tip of the Malay Peninsula.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.890
And Jordan, in Western Asia.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.770
Singapore has about 106 cubic metres of
renewable fresh water per person a year;

5
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.930
Jordan, about 61.

6
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.410
Both far below 500.

7
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.410
Both import most of their food and energy.

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.750
So which is more resource-secure?

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.210
Or are they equally insecure?

10
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.950
Can it even be judged?

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.990
In this mission, you'll
take each country apart:

12
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.890
its water, its food, its energy.

13
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.290
Then you'll judge two big answers:
recycled NEWater in Singapore,

14
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:46.770
and a planned 450 kilometre pipeline
of desalinated Red Sea water to Amman.

15
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.450
Your mission: decide which
country is more resource-secure,

16
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.510
and justify your choice.
